{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When your son asks you tomorrow, saying: What is the testimony and the statutes and the ordinances.</b> That is to say: why were we commanded concerning very many commandments in these three categories? And you shall say to your son: 'We were slaves to Pharaoh in Egypt,' and out of the affliction and bondage the Holy One, blessed be He, brought us out from there and performed renowned miracles for us; therefore we are greatly indebted to Him and bound to accept the yoke of His commandments. And this answer to this question is Torah, for the remembrance of the exodus from Egypt is the root of the Torah and a great principal and foundation for all the commandments, every one of them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:09.773190833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}